From: klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:51:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipc: hyprctl keyword and the 0.56 dispatch form, on the Lua
 configuration

0.57 dropped the keyword command and reads dispatch as hl.dispatch(<lua>), so
every WolOS tool that set an option, a bind or a window rule live, or sent a
0.56 dispatcher (theme switch, Settings, zoom, overview, switcher, the Dock,
hypridle), got an error. keyword NAME VALUE becomes the Lua call it means
(hl.config with a typed literal, hl.bind/hl.unbind, hl.animation, the named
rule's hl.window_rule) and runs like eval; dispatch NAME ARGS with a 0.56
dispatcher name runs it through the 0.56 translator, back on Config::Actions;
keyword binds call it through hl.legacy_dispatch. Lua forms are unchanged.
Translation in WolosCompat.hpp, gtest in tests/helpers/WolosCompat.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
